concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-130 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "130 Application of the Australian Consumer Law in relation to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-130 ;
    values:originalText "corporations  The Australian Consumer Law applies as a law of the Commonwealth to the conduct of corporations. 131  Division does not apply to financial services etc.  (1) Despite section 130, this Division does not apply to the supply, or possible supply, of services that are financial services.  (2) Despite section 130, Part 2 of the Australian Consumer Law does not apply to, or in relation to:  (a) contracts that are financial products; or  (b) contracts for the supply, or possible supply, of services that are financial services." ;
    skos:definition "corporations  The Australian Consumer Law applies as a law of the Commonwealth to the conduct of corporations. 131  Division does not apply to financial services etc.  (1) Despite section 130, this Division does not apply to the supply, or possible supply, of services that are financial services.  (2) Despite section 130, Part 2 of the Australian Consumer Law does not apply to, or in relation to:  (a) contracts that are financial products; or  (b) contracts for the supply, or possible supply, of services that are financial services."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9c66a97a80045cd4c4f41d96adbc1fd54c1d87c2bb0db77093ea21221849c1e2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "17"^^xsd:integer ;
