concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-135 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135 The applied Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-135 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The applied Australian Consumer Law consists of:  (a) Schedule 2; and  (b) the remaining provisions of this Act (except sections 2A, 4KB, 5, 6 and 172), so far as they relate to Schedule 2; and  (c) the regulations under this Act, so far as they relate to any provision covered by paragraph (a) or (b).  (2) For the purpose of forming part of the applied Australian Consumer Law, the provisions referred to in paragraphs (1)(b) and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The applied Australian Consumer Law consists of:  (a) Schedule 2; and  (b) the remaining provisions of this Act (except sections 2A, 4KB, 5, 6 and 172), so far as they relate to Schedule 2; and  (c) the regulations under this Act, so far as they relate to any provision covered by paragraph (a) or (b).  (2) For the purpose of forming part of the applied Australian Consumer Law, the provisions referred to in paragraphs (1)(b) and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f95ee12f41e4b9e5c153cc9f4f6ce71acb327a67ebe86e6c37cf6697e3ea7012" ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-135-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-135-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act.pdf, p.19" .
doc:sch-2-sec-135 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "135 The applied Australian Consumer Law" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The applied Australian Consumer Law consists of:  (a) Schedule 2; and  (b) the remaining provisions of this Act (except sections 2A, 4KB, 5, 6 and 172), so far as they relate to Schedule 2; and  (c) the regulations under this Act, so far as they relate to any provision covered by paragraph (a) or (b).  (2) For the purpose of forming part of the applied Australian Consumer Law, the provisions referred to in paragraphs (1)(b) and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Schedule 1  The Australian Consumer Law" ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer .

