concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-136 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "136 Federal Court may exercise jurisdiction under application laws"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-136 ;
    values:originalText "of Territories  The Federal Court may exercise jurisdiction (whether original or appellate) conferred on that Court by an application law of a Territory with respect to matters arising under the applied Australian Consumer Law." ;
