doc:sch-2-sec-142-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "142(2) No doubling-up of liabilities" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If a person has been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty under an application law, the person is not liable to a pecuniary penalty under this Act in respect of the same conduct." ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-143 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "143 References in instruments to the Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-143 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A reference in any instrument to the Australian Consumer Law is a reference to:  (a) the Australian Consumer Law as applied under Division 1; and  (b) the applied Australian Consumer Laws of any or all of the participating jurisdictions. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1 Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Part 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (2) Subsection (1) has effect except so far as the contrary intention appears in the instrument or the context of the reference otherwise requires. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Schedule 2  Enforcement and remedies under the Trade Practices Act 1974" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A reference in any instrument to the Australian Consumer Law is a reference to:  (a) the Australian Consumer Law as applied under Division 1; and  (b) the applied Australian Consumer Laws of any or all of the participating jurisdictions. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  The Australian Consumer Law  Schedule 1 Application of the Australian Consumer Law  Part 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (2) Subsection (1) has effect except so far as the contrary intention appears in the instrument or the context of the reference otherwise requires. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Schedule 2  Enforcement and remedies under the Trade Practices Act 1974"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f76118accf998766313b1d005f2e2d3f098905944bf0655cc52bc813dd420e67" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
