doc:sch-2-sec-76e-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "76E(1) Pecuniary penalties—consumer protection etc." ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Court is satisfied that a person:  (a) has contravened any of the following provisions:  (i) a provision of Part IVA;  (ii) a provision of Division 1 or 1AAA of Part V (other than section 52);  (iii) subsection 65C(1) or (3), 65D(1) or 65F(8), section 65G or subsection 65Q(9), (9C) or (10) or 65R(1);  (iv) section 87ZN or 87ZO; or  (b) has attempted to contravene such a provision; or  (c) has aided, abetted, counselled or procured a person to contravene such a provision; or  (d) has induced, or attempted to induce, a person, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, to contravene such a provision; or  (e) has been in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, the contravention by a person of such a provision; or  (f) has conspired with others to contravene such a provision; the Court may order the person to pay to the Commonwealth such pecuniary penalty, in respect of each act or omission by the person to which this section applies, as the Court determines to be appropriate." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-76e-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "76E(2) Pecuniary penalties—consumer protection etc."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-76e-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) In determining the appropriate pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard to all relevant matters including: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Enforcement and remedies under the Trade Practices Act 1974  Schedule 2 Pecuniary penalties  Part 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (a) the nature and extent of the act or omission and of any loss or damage suffered as a result of the act or omission; and  (b) the circumstances in which the act or omission took place; and  (c) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in proceedings under Part VC or this Part to have engaged in any similar conduct." ;
    skos:definition "(2) In determining the appropriate pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard to all relevant matters including: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Enforcement and remedies under the Trade Practices Act 1974  Schedule 2 Pecuniary penalties  Part 1  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (a) the nature and extent of the act or omission and of any loss or damage suffered as a result of the act or omission; and  (b) the circumstances in which the act or omission took place; and  (c) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in proceedings under Part VC or this Part to have engaged in any similar conduct."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "001834afdb89a17cd4fef9e45703e86e845c6b8bf01e9c05550c7b6cc21b17ed" ;
