doc:sch-2-sec-76f-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "76F(2) Pecuniary penalties under section 76E and offences" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Proceedings for an order under section 76E against a person in relation to a consumer protection breach are stayed if:  (a) criminal proceedings are started or have already been started against the person for an offence; and  (b) the offence is constituted by conduct that is substantially the same as the conduct alleged to constitute the consumer protection breach. The proceedings for the order may be resumed if the person is not convicted of the offence. Otherwise, the proceedings are dismissed." ;
