doc:sch-2-sec-18-2-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "18(1) After section 87" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Without limiting the generality of section 80, if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Enforcement and remedies under the Trade Practices Act 1974  Schedule 2 Orders to redress loss or damage suffered by non-party consumers etc.  Part 4  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (a) a person engaged in conduct (the contravening conduct) in contravention of a provision of Part IVA, of Division 1 or 1AAA of Part V or of Part VC; and  (b) the contravening conduct caused, or is likely to cause, a class of persons to suffer loss or damage; and  (c) the class includes persons who are non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct; the Court may, on the application of the Commission, make such order or orders (other than an award of damages) as the Court thinks appropriate against a person referred to in subsection (2) of this section. Note: The orders that the Court may make include all or any of the orders set out in section 87AAB." ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-18-2-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18(2) After section 87"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-18-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) An order under subsection (1) may be made against the person who engaged in the contravening conduct or a person involved in that conduct." ;
    skos:definition "(2) An order under subsection (1) may be made against the person who engaged in the contravening conduct or a person involved in that conduct."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9e463836bbc8253a2382fb51a8278e8e4e4217c7b1fb3464ffbe395421728212" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-18-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Order against person involved in contravening conduct" ;
