concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-18-2-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18(3) After section 87"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-18-2-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Court must not make an order under subsection (1) unless the Court considers that the order will:  (a) redress, in whole or in part, the loss or damage suffered by the non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct; or  (b) prevent or reduce the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by the non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct. Application for orders" ;
    skos:definition "(3) The Court must not make an order under subsection (1) unless the Court considers that the order will:  (a) redress, in whole or in part, the loss or damage suffered by the non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct; or  (b) prevent or reduce the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by the non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct. Application for orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d8d95a1d414d662dc9b27faf5b71cfa7b5c70c87e2b5a959f7c406f8b81c5bea" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-18-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Court must consider redressing or preventing loss/damage to non-party consumers before making an order." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act.pdf> ;
