    cml:modality cml:LTL ;
    cml:operator "Recurring trace" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Redress, prevention, or reduction of loss or damage repeated." ;
    cml:premiseText "Redress, prevention, or reduction of loss or damage is redressed, prevented or reduced in accordance with the order." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Redress, prevention, or reduction of loss or damage is repeated." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::temporal_ltl" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-32-ss-9 cml:asserts concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-32-ss-9-logic-deontic-5 .
concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-32-ss-9-logic-deontic-5 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Obligation" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Non-party consumer bound by order if conditions are met." ;
    cml:premiseText "(a) an order is made under subsection (1) against a person; and (b) the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by a non-party consumer in relation to the contravening conduct..." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Non-party consumer is bound by the order if conditions are met." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-32-ss-9 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32(9) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44," ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(9) If:  (a) an order is made under subsection (1) against a person; and  (b) the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by a non-party consumer in relation to the contravening conduct to which the order relates has been redressed, prevented or reduced in accordance with the order; and  (c) the non-party consumer has accepted the redress, prevention or reduction; then:  (d) the non-party consumer is bound by the order; and  (e) any other order made under subsection (1) that relates to that loss or damage has no effect in relation to the non-party consumer; and  (f) despite any other provision of this Act or any other law of the Commonwealth, or a State or Territory, no claim, action or demand may be made or taken against the person by the non-party consumer in relation to that loss or damage. Other" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-32-ss-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32(10) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-32-ss-10 ;
    values:originalText "(10) Subsection (1) has effect subject to section 87AB. Note: Section 87AB may limit the liability, under an order made under subsection (1) of this section, of a person for his or her contravention of section 52 (which is about misleading or deceptive conduct) or involvement in such a contravention." ;
    skos:definition "(10) Subsection (1) has effect subject to section 87AB. Note: Section 87AB may limit the liability, under an order made under subsection (1) of this section, of a person for his or her contravention of section 52 (which is about misleading or deceptive conduct) or involvement in such a contravention."@en ;
