doc:sch-2-sec-87ze-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "87ZE(3) Issue of an infringement notice" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The infringement notice does not have any effect if the notice:  (a) is issued more than 12 months after the day on which the contravention of the infringement notice provision is alleged to have occurred; or  (b) relates to more than one alleged contravention of an infringement notice provision by the person." ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-87zf a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "87ZF Matters to be included in an infringement notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-87zf ;
    values:originalText "An infringement notice must:  (a) be identified by a unique number; and  (b) state the day on which it is issued; and  (c) state the name and address of the person to whom it is issued; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Enforcement and remedies under the Trade Practices Act 1974  Schedule 2 Infringement notices  Part 5  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (d) state that it is being issued by the Commission; and  (e) state how the Commission may be contacted; and  (f) give details of the alleged contravention by the person, including:  (i) the date of the alleged contravention; and  (ii) the particular infringement notice provision that was allegedly contravened; and  (g) state the maximum pecuniary penalty that the Court could order the person to pay under section 76E for the alleged contravention; and  (h) specify the penalty that is payable in relation to the alleged contravention; and  (i) state that the penalty is payable within the infringement notice compliance period for the notice; and  (j) state that the penalty is payable to the Commission on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (k) explain how payment of the penalty is to be made; and  (l) explain the effect of sections 87ZH, 87ZI, 87ZJ and 87ZK." ;
    skos:definition "An infringement notice must:  (a) be identified by a unique number; and  (b) state the day on which it is issued; and  (c) state the name and address of the person to whom it is issued; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Enforcement and remedies under the Trade Practices Act 1974  Schedule 2 Infringement notices  Part 5  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (d) state that it is being issued by the Commission; and  (e) state how the Commission may be contacted; and  (f) give details of the alleged contravention by the person, including:  (i) the date of the alleged contravention; and  (ii) the particular infringement notice provision that was allegedly contravened; and  (g) state the maximum pecuniary penalty that the Court could order the person to pay under section 76E for the alleged contravention; and  (h) specify the penalty that is payable in relation to the alleged contravention; and  (i) state that the penalty is payable within the infringement notice compliance period for the notice; and  (j) state that the penalty is payable to the Commission on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (k) explain how payment of the penalty is to be made; and  (l) explain the effect of sections 87ZH, 87ZI, 87ZJ and 87ZK."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5787b072c79af3ba3238831742e20d8a1c4cb6cb17d51fc0c5f07aa9b6309f1c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Infringement notice requirements" ;
    dc:description "a unique number, day of issue, name and address, Commission contact details, alleged contravention details, penalty information, payment instructions" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
