doc:sch-2-sec-87zk-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "87ZK(5) Withdrawal of an infringement notice" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) The withdrawal notice must state:  (a) the name and address of the person; and  (b) the day on which the infringement notice was issued to the person; and  (c) that the infringement notice is withdrawn; and  (d) that proceedings under Part VC or VI may be started or continued against the person in relation to:  (i) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice provision; or  (ii) an offence constituted by the same conduct that constituted the alleged contravention. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Enforcement and remedies under the Trade Practices Act 1974  Schedule 2 Infringement notices  Part 5  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010 Time limit for giving withdrawal notices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-2-sec-87zk-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "87ZK(6) Withdrawal of an infringement notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-87zk-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) To be effective, the withdrawal notice must be given to the person within the infringement notice compliance period for the infringement notice. Refunds" ;
    skos:definition "(6) To be effective, the withdrawal notice must be given to the person within the infringement notice compliance period for the infringement notice. Refunds"@en ;
