doc:sch-3-sec-56-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56(4) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44," ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If conduct constitutes a contravention of 2 or more provisions referred to in paragraph (1)(a):  (a) a proceeding may be instituted under this Act against a person in relation to the contravention of any one or more of the provisions; but  (b) a person is not liable to more than one pecuniary penalty under this section in respect of the same conduct. 12GBB  Pecuniary penalties and offences" ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-56-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56(1) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-56-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Court must not make an order under section 12GBA against a person in relation to either of the following matters (a consumer protection breach):  (a) a contravention of a provision referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(a);  (b) conduct referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) that relates to a contravention of a provision referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(a); ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Amendment of corporations legislation  Schedule 3 Pecuniary penalties  Part 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010 if the person has been convicted of an offence constituted by conduct that is substantially the same as the conduct constituting the consumer protection breach." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Court must not make an order under section 12GBA against a person in relation to either of the following matters (a consumer protection breach):  (a) a contravention of a provision referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(a);  (b) conduct referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) that relates to a contravention of a provision referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(a); ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Amendment of corporations legislation  Schedule 3 Pecuniary penalties  Part 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010 if the person has been convicted of an offence constituted by conduct that is substantially the same as the conduct constituting the consumer protection breach."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "92752172a82ae3637911f30dccd4056950387afae12ba2dfeb3d7b33706df942" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-56 ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court cannot make an order under section 12GBA against a person in relation to certain consumer protection breaches. Commonwealth may recover pecuniary penalty from ASIC." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
