doc:sch-3-sec-56-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56(1) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44," ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Court must not make an order under section 12GBA against a person in relation to either of the following matters (a consumer protection breach):  (a) a contravention of a provision referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(a);  (b) conduct referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) that relates to a contravention of a provision referred to in paragraph 12GBA(1)(a); ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Amendment of corporations legislation  Schedule 3 Pecuniary penalties  Part 2  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010 if the person has been convicted of an offence constituted by conduct that is substantially the same as the conduct constituting the consumer protection breach." ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-56-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56(2) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-56-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Proceedings for an order under section 12GBA against a person in relation to a consumer protection breach are stayed if:  (a) criminal proceedings are started or have already been started against the person for an offence; and  (b) the offence is constituted by conduct that is substantially the same as the conduct alleged to constitute the consumer protection breach. The proceedings for the order may be resumed if the person is not convicted of the offence. Otherwise, the proceedings are dismissed." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Proceedings for an order under section 12GBA against a person in relation to a consumer protection breach are stayed if:  (a) criminal proceedings are started or have already been started against the person for an offence; and  (b) the offence is constituted by conduct that is substantially the same as the conduct alleged to constitute the consumer protection breach. The proceedings for the order may be resumed if the person is not convicted of the offence. Otherwise, the proceedings are dismissed."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6365d6a40bd33e39e42535425e9a6b4c1b2bf51e70809742e17f9565af75dca5" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-56 ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Time limit for commencing a proceeding under subsection (1) Proceedings for an order under section 12GBA are stayed if criminal proceedings are started or have already been started against the person for an offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
