doc:sch-3-sec-56-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56(3) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44," ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Criminal proceedings may be started against a person for conduct that is substantially the same as conduct constituting a consumer protection breach regardless of whether an order under section 12GBA has been made against the person in respect of the breach." ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-56-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56(4) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-56-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Evidence of information given, or evidence of production of documents, by an individual is not admissible in criminal proceedings against the individual if:  (a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the documents in proceedings for an order under section 12GBA against the individual in relation to a consumer protection breach (whether or not the order was made); and  (b) the conduct alleged to constitute the offence is substantially the same as the conduct that was claimed to constitute the consumer protection breach. However, this does not apply to a criminal proceeding in respect of the falsity of the evidence given by the individual in the proceedings for the order. 12GBC  Civil action for recovery of pecuniary penalties" ;
    skos:definition "(4) Evidence of information given, or evidence of production of documents, by an individual is not admissible in criminal proceedings against the individual if:  (a) the individual previously gave the evidence or produced the documents in proceedings for an order under section 12GBA against the individual in relation to a consumer protection breach (whether or not the order was made); and  (b) the conduct alleged to constitute the offence is substantially the same as the conduct that was claimed to constitute the consumer protection breach. However, this does not apply to a criminal proceeding in respect of the falsity of the evidence given by the individual in the proceedings for the order. 12GBC  Civil action for recovery of pecuniary penalties"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ddf6ac1d79632f088825f86387d632d29fca159f0dff56d1118f464567ff82b9" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-56 ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "No more than one pecuniary penalty for the same conduct. Prevents reusing evidence in criminal proceedings for substantially the same conduct as a previous consumer protection breach order." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act.pdf> ;
