concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-58-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "58(5) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-58-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If, as a result of the operation of Part 2.4 of the Criminal Code, a person other than a body corporate is:  (a) convicted of an offence (the relevant offence) against subsection (1) of this section; or  (b) convicted of an offence (the relevant offence) against section 11.4 of the Criminal Code in relation to an offence referred to in subsection (1) of this section; the relevant offence is taken to be punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 5 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "(5) If, as a result of the operation of Part 2.4 of the Criminal Code, a person other than a body corporate is:  (a) convicted of an offence (the relevant offence) against subsection (1) of this section; or  (b) convicted of an offence (the relevant offence) against section 11.4 of the Criminal Code in relation to an offence referred to in subsection (1) of this section; the relevant offence is taken to be punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 5 penalty units."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "540dcd7eaa3a39c3f76f50d9a472ae66ef19a1de85bf42ba9ee8249e5c533df7" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-58 ;
