concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-13 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13 Subsection 12GLB(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-13 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) The Court may, on application by ASIC, make an adverse publicity order in relation to a person who:  (a) has been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty under section 12GBA; or  (b) is guilty of an offence under section 12GB. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Schedule 3  Amendment of corporations legislation" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) The Court may, on application by ASIC, make an adverse publicity order in relation to a person who:  (a) has been ordered to pay a pecuniary penalty under section 12GBA; or  (b) is guilty of an offence under section 12GB. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Schedule 3  Amendment of corporations legislation"@en ;
