or representation made by the person if the person:  (a) is a prescribed information provider within the meaning of section 12DN; and  (b) made the claim or representation by publishing it on behalf of another person in the course of carrying on a business of providing information; and  (c) does not have a commercial relationship with the other person other than for the purpose of:  (i) publishing claims or representations promoting, or apparently intended to promote, the other person’s business or other activities; or  (ii) the other person supplying financial services to the person. 12GYA  Extending periods for complying with substantiation notices  (1) A person who has been given a substantiation notice may, at any time within 21 days after the notice was given to the person, apply ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Schedule 3  Amendment of corporations legislation" ;
