concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-20-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20(6) Before Subdivision H of Division 2 of Part 2"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-20-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) This section does not apply to a person in relation to a claim or representation made by the person if the person:  (a) is a prescribed information provider within the meaning of section 12DN; and  (b) made the claim or representation by publishing it on behalf of another person in the course of carrying on a business of providing information; and  (c) does not have a commercial relationship with the other person other than for the purpose of:  (i) publishing claims or representations promoting, or apparently intended to promote, the other person’s business or other activities; or  (ii) the other person supplying financial services to the person. 12GYA  Extending periods for complying with substantiation notices" ;
    skos:definition "(6) This section does not apply to a person in relation to a claim or representation made by the person if the person:  (a) is a prescribed information provider within the meaning of section 12DN; and  (b) made the claim or representation by publishing it on behalf of another person in the course of carrying on a business of providing information; and  (c) does not have a commercial relationship with the other person other than for the purpose of:  (i) publishing claims or representations promoting, or apparently intended to promote, the other person’s business or other activities; or  (ii) the other person supplying financial services to the person. 12GYA  Extending periods for complying with substantiation notices"@en ;
