concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-64-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "64(3) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-64-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Despite subsection (1), an individual may refuse or fail to give particular information or produce a particular document in compliance with a substantiation notice on the ground that the information or production of the document might tend to incriminate the individual or to expose the individual to a penalty. 12GYC  False or misleading information etc." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Despite subsection (1), an individual may refuse or fail to give particular information or produce a particular document in compliance with a substantiation notice on the ground that the information or production of the document might tend to incriminate the individual or to expose the individual to a penalty. 12GYC  False or misleading information etc."@en ;
