concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-66-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "66(6) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-66-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (1) against a person referred to in subsection (2), the Court may have regard to the conduct of the person, and of the non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct, since the contravention occurred. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Amendment of corporations legislation  Schedule 3 Orders to redress loss or damage suffered by non-party consumers etc.  Part 5  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010" ;
    skos:definition "(6) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (1) against a person referred to in subsection (2), the Court may have regard to the conduct of the person, and of the non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct, since the contravention occurred. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Amendment of corporations legislation  Schedule 3 Orders to redress loss or damage suffered by non-party consumers etc.  Part 5  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3c21b9fa64e54ca77a81d6dc9006ab614ce1ce373988f1702bb734b5e766f943" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-66 ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Consider conduct of person and non-party consumers in determining whether to make an order under subsection (1)" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act.pdf, p.70" ;
    cml:asserts concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-66-ss-6-norm .
