doc:sch-3-sec-66-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "66(6) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44," ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (1) against a person referred to in subsection (2), the Court may have regard to the conduct of the person, and of the non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct, since the contravention occurred. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Amendment of corporations legislation  Schedule 3 Orders to redress loss or damage suffered by non-party consumers etc.  Part 5  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010" ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-66-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "66(8) Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-66-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (1), the Court need not make a finding about either of the following matters:  (a) which persons are non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct;  (b) the nature of the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by such persons. When a non-party consumer is bound by an order etc." ;
    skos:definition "(8) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (1), the Court need not make a finding about either of the following matters:  (a) which persons are non-party consumers in relation to the contravening conduct;  (b) the nature of the loss or damage suffered, or likely to be suffered, by such persons. When a non-party consumer is bound by an order etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b40ac160b70bd1a7960e1a0c7b994df9aac3c8574538ed856f2fe4a296b574a5" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-66 ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court does not need to determine non-party consumers or nature of loss/damage in making an order." ;
