doc:sch-3-sec-12gx-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "12GX(1) Purpose and effect of this Subdivision" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The purpose of this Subdivision is to provide for the issue of an infringement notice to a person for an alleged contravention of an infringement notice provision as an alternative to proceedings for an order under section 12GBA." ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer .

concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-12gx-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12GX(2) Purpose and effect of this Subdivision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-12gx-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) This Subdivision does not:  (a) require an infringement notice to be issued to a person for an alleged contravention of an infringement notice provision; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Amendment of corporations legislation  Schedule 3 Infringement notices  Part 6  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (b) affect the liability of a person to proceedings under Subdivision G (sections 12GA to 12GO) in relation to an alleged contravention of an infringement notice provision if:  (i) an infringement notice is not issued to the person for the alleged contravention; or  (ii) an infringement notice issued to a person for the alleged contravention is withdrawn under section 12GXG; or  (c) prevent a Court from imposing a higher penalty than the penalty specified in the infringement notice if the person does not comply with the notice. 12GXA  Issue of an infringement notice" ;
    skos:definition "(2) This Subdivision does not:  (a) require an infringement notice to be issued to a person for an alleged contravention of an infringement notice provision; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2010A00044  Amendment of corporations legislation  Schedule 3 Infringement notices  Part 6  Trade Practices Amendment (Australian Consumer Law) Act (No. 1) 2010       No. 44, 2010  (b) affect the liability of a person to proceedings under Subdivision G (sections 12GA to 12GO) in relation to an alleged contravention of an infringement notice provision if:  (i) an infringement notice is not issued to the person for the alleged contravention; or  (ii) an infringement notice issued to a person for the alleged contravention is withdrawn under section 12GXG; or  (c) prevent a Court from imposing a higher penalty than the penalty specified in the infringement notice if the person does not comply with the notice. 12GXA  Issue of an infringement notice"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "28e2a8c8645ba1356c2bceab2b951671c32bd00a037400df4a9e74ed5930d768" ;
    values:partOf concept:trade-practices-amendment-australian-consumer-law-act-sch-3-sec-12gx ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "ASIC must not issue more than one infringement notice for the same alleged contravention. No infringement notice required for alleged contravention of infringement notice provision" ;
